  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Additional COVID-19 Investments via HEPRTF World Bank</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The country Zimbabwe seeks to vaccinate all eligible population   from 12 years and above.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project development objective (PDO) is to support the Government of Zimbabwe to deploy and manage COVID-19 vaccines and strengthen related health system capacity.
The following indicators will be used to measure the achievement of the PDO:
1. Percentage of population vaccinated which is included in the priority population as defined in the national plan, disaggregated by gender  
2. Proportion of primary health care facilities with functional solar-powered cold chain system</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is part of an expanded health response to the pandemic, which is being supported by development partners (DPs), including the World Bank, under the coordination of the GOZ. This additional World Bank financing provides essential resources to expand a sustained and comprehensive pandemic response that includes vaccine deployment and climate friendly related health system strengthening in Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </description>
